{
  "name": "alloptical_nand",
  "description": "All-optical NAND by cross-gain modulation in a semiconductor optical amplifier: light switches light. A weak 1550 nm probe shares an SOA with two 1310 nm control beams (inputs A and B, each a laser that is on = 1 / off = 0). The controls are combined losslessly on a PBS (A is V, B is H) and folded onto the probe by a dichroic. Every photon through the SOA competes for the same gain, so the controls darken the probe; one control halves the probe level, both together saturate the gain. A second dichroic dumps the 1310 nm controls, and a saturable absorber squares away the residual probe in the both-on case. OUT is bright unless A AND B.",
